### 8\. Delta sync me performance bug

High priority

RPC:

`delta_sync_pull(...)`

Isme task fetch kuch aisa hai:

```sql
select coalesce(
    jsonb_agg(to_jsonb(t) order by t.updated_at desc),
    '[]'::jsonb
)
into v_tasks
from public.tasks t
where public.can_view_task(t.id)
limit 200;
```

Problem: aggregate query pe `LIMIT 200` lagane se underlying 200 task rows select nahi hote.

Pehle aggregate ek JSON result row banata hai. `LIMIT 200` us single result row par apply hota hai.

Matlab 200 tasks ka cap effectively nahi laga.

Isi tarah incidents aur notifications ke fetch me bhi issue hai.

### Correct SQL pattern

Pehle subquery me rows limit karo, phir aggregate:

```sql
select coalesce(
    jsonb_agg(to_jsonb(x) order by x.updated_at desc),
    '[]'::jsonb
)
into v_tasks
from (
    select t.*
    from public.tasks t
    where public.can_view_task(t.id)
      and (
          v_effective_since is null
          or t.updated_at >= v_effective_since
      )
    order by t.updated_at desc
    limit 200
) x;
```

Incidents aur notifications ke liye bhi same pattern chahiye.

Ye fix nahi hua to large database me delta sync payload bahut bada ho sakta hai.

### 9\. Supabase Realtime: implementation hai, guarantee nahi

File:

`TaskzRealtimeManager.kt`

Positive points:

* Foreground-only WebSocket connection

* Background me disconnect

* Reconnect backoff

* Duplicate event cache

* Role switch par reconnect

* Heartbeat

Ye battery ke liye achha direction hai.

### Lekin 4 issues hain

1\. Broad subscriptions

Tasks aur incidents ke subscriptions me filter null hai:

```kotlin
Triple("realtime:tasks_$currentRoleCode", "tasks", null)
Triple("realtime:incidents_$currentRoleCode", "system_incidents", null)
```

Isse device broad table subscriptions request karta hai. RLS server-side access ko restrict kar sakti hai, lekin unnecessary subscription traffic aur server workload ka risk hai.

2\. Join acknowledgement verify nahi hota

Code `phx_join` send karta hai, lekin `phx_reply` status ko properly inspect karke channel join success confirm nahi karta.

WebSocket open hona aur database subscription successfully join hona alag hai.

Abhi `isConnected=true` socket open par set hota hai. Isse UI ya sync coordinator ko false impression mil sakta hai ki realtime fully operational hai.

3\. Subscription errors detect nahi hote

Channel join reject ho jaaye to system ko clear failure state aur retry/recovery chahiye.

4\. Reconnect attempts limit

Maximum reconnect attempts 6 hain. Uske baad connection tab tak restore nahi hoga jab tak koi later lifecycle/session event retry trigger na kare.

Network stable hone par explicit recovery path chahiye.

Recommendation: official supported Supabase Realtime client/protocol integration ya custom WebSocket ka complete protocol-level test. Har channel ka join acknowledgement, token refresh, reconnect, role change aur subscription failure test karo.

### 10\. Offline sync: architecture achha hai, concurrency verify karni hogi

Files:

* `TaskzSyncManager.kt`

* `SyncWorker.kt`

* `OutboxDao.kt`

* `OutboxEventEntity.kt`

* `SyncMetadataDao.kt`

Positive points:

* Persistent Room outbox

* Pending operation IDs

* Retry status

* Network constraints

* Exponential backoff

* Server acknowledgement state

* Delta pull

* Role/scope cache invalidation

Ye implementation ka strong part hai.

### Lekin sync ke do parallel paths hain

* `TaskzSyncManager.syncNow()`

* `SyncWorker.doWork()`

Dono task/incident pending operations process kar sakte hain.

`TaskzSyncManager` ke paas process-level `syncMutex` hai, lekin Worker ka alag execution path hai. Dono ke beech ek shared database-level atomic claim/lease mechanism clearly verify karna zaroori hai.

Duplicate request ke liye backend idempotency bhi har mutation par honi chahiye.

### WorkManager me ek aur observation

Periodic sync 15 minutes par schedule hai:

```kotlin
PeriodicWorkRequestBuilder<SyncWorker>(15, TimeUnit.MINUTES)
```

Network reconnect par immediate work bhi enqueue hota hai.

Periodic fallback reasonable hai, lekin periodic aur immediate jobs ki concurrency, duplicate processing aur unnecessary wakeups test hone chahiye.

`ExistingWorkPolicy.REPLACE` immediate work ko replace kar sakta hai. Running worker cancel hone par pending outbox durable rehni chahiye—ye sahi tarah verify karo.

Required fix: one shared durable outbox claim mechanism, atomic state transitions, worker concurrency test, aur sync cursor tabhi advance ho jab actual server reconciliation successful ho.

### 11\. Device token and logout handling

`DeviceTokenManager` me multi-device design ka direction achha hai.

* device ID

* device-specific token

* device-specific deactivation

* same account ke multiple phones ka support

Lekin actual FCM token nahi milne par local fallback token register ho raha hai. Isse backend ke `device_tokens` records me invalid push tokens aa sakte hain.

Logout path me `TaskzSyncManager.onLogout()` realtime disconnect aur local cache clear karta hai. Lekin is method ke andar `deviceTokenManager.deactivateThisDeviceOnly()` ka call nahi dikha.

Ye verify karna hai ki actual logout repository flow me ye deactivation kahin aur hoti hai ya nahi.

Required fix: FCM token ke bina push registration mat karo. Logout par current device token deactivate karo, doosre logged-in devices ko touch mat karo.

